# Introduction
Students’ academic performance is an important issue in education, as it influences future educational and labor market outcomes. 

This project analyzes a dataset on students’ exam scores combined with demographic characteristics, study behavior, and school-related factors. The objective is to identify the main determinants of exam performance using linear regression models.

The analysis is conducted in several steps:

- Data preparation and cleaning to ensure consistency and proper coding of variables.
- Exploratory data analysis (EDA) to describe the data and guide model specification.
- Estimation and comparison of multiple linear regression models using statistical criteria.
- Diagnostic checks to assess model assumptions and robustness.
- Evaluation of predictive performance using a validation approach.


